  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `195dfcc5b541` symmetry/order prototype\nTask/source: generator `3.0.0`, SHA-256 `af8350048eca44100de1d539ba7bb3f295bb82cbf99411f7eef218c4c1e56ed7`; canonical rule `22e420574f26`.\nScope: proposed task-local prototype only; the production generator and canonical Racket ledger are unchanged.\nDefect \u2192 build: production examples teach reflection but isolate copies, so overlap-order tie-breaking is unobservable; added episode-fixed reflection and column-order parameters over a controlled overlap motif.\nDefault preservation: `(dihedral, left_to_right)` is byte-for-byte the canonical Racket program and replays all five canonical labels exactly.\nLesson contract: each of four settings has three demonstrations and four distinct queries; demonstrations reject all three declared rivals before query answers are used.\nFocused checks: `57 passed` through the protected Racket wrapper; the unwrapped diagnostic produced `54 passed, 3 unavailable` because no protected Racket executable was injected.\nExact evidence: 28 stored labels, 84 rival labels, and five canonical labels matched Racket; all 48 demo-only query/rival checks passed; four public challenges are masked and uniquely content-addressed.\nAdversarial evidence: 32 seeds \u00d7 four settings yielded 128 episodes/256 pairs with zero failures; 16+16 counts, public-ID privacy, and a second Racket seed base passed.\nTickets: both bounded supplementary tickets completed; neither created a safety finding or `AUDIT.md`.\nRemaining limits: finite four-setting evidence, one controlled 2\u00d74 overlap motif, and no production approval, training admission, or closure of the historical production overlap audit.\nDisposition: routine prototype handoff; any production promotion remains needs-attention and should preserve the source/rule separation above.",
